<entry><id>tag:rss.naad-adna.pelmorex.com,2026-11-06:feed.atom/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.124.3601961978.2026</id><title>yellow advisory - freezing drizzle - in effect</title><updated>2026-11-06T17:21:51-00:00</updated><author><name>Environment Canada</name></author><link href="http://capcp2.naad-adna.pelmorex.com/2026-11-06/2026_11_06T17_21_51_00_00Iurn_oid_2.49.0.1.124.3601961978.2026.xml" rel="alternate"/><georss:polygon>61.9997 -138.2519 61.6684 -139.6387 61.3998 -141.0017 63.1831 -141.0021 63.1831 -141.0013 63.1824 -139.6454 63.1167 -138.252 62.5518 -138.1789 61.9997 -138.2519</georss:polygon><summary type="html">Description: Areas of freezing drizzle are expected.

When: Now until this afternoon.

Where: Beaver Creek

Remarks:
Periods of freezing drizzle and light snow will continue near Beaver Creek for the rest of today. Conditions are expected to improve late this afternoon.

###

Roads, walkways, and other surfaces will likely become icy and slippery. Icy surfaces will likely form and could be difficult to detect.

Please continue to monitor alerts and forecasts issued by Environment Canada. To report severe weather, send an email to YTstorm@ec.gc.ca or post reports on social media using #YTStorm.&lt;br&gt;Expires: 2026-11-07T02:20:51-00:00&lt;br&gt;Originated from CAP Alert: Environment Canada, 2026-11-06T17:21:51-00:00, urn:oid:2.49.0.1.124.3601961978.2026&lt;br&gt;Area: Beaver Creek</summary><category term="status=Actual"/><category term="msgType=Alert"/><category term="scope=Public"/><category term="language=en-CA"/><category term="category=Met"/><category term="severity=Moderate"/><category term="urgency=Immediate"/><category term="certainty=Likely"/><category term="event=freezing drizzle"/></entry>
<entry><id>tag:rss.naad-adna.pelmorex.com,2026-11-06:feed.atom/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.124.3601961978.2026</id><title>avis jaune - bruine verglaçante - en vigueur</title><updated>2026-11-06T17:21:51-00:00</updated><author><name>Environnement Canada</name></author><link href="http://capcp2.naad-adna.pelmorex.com/2026-11-06/2026_11_06T17_21_51_00_00Iurn_oid_2.49.0.1.124.3601961978.2026.xml" rel="alternate"/><georss:polygon>61.9997 -138.2519 61.6684 -139.6387 61.3998 -141.0017 63.1831 -141.0021 63.1831 -141.0013 63.1824 -139.6454 63.1167 -138.252 62.5518 -138.1789 61.9997 -138.2519</georss:polygon><summary type="html">Description: De la bruine verglaçante est prévue par endroits.

Quand : à compter de maintenant et jusqu'en après-midi.

Où : Beaver Creek

Remarques :
De la bruine verglaçante passagère et de la faible neige persisteront près de Beaver Creek pour le reste de la journée. Les conditions devraient s'améliorer en fin d'après-midi.

###

Les routes, les trottoirs et les autres surfaces deviendront probablement glacés et glissants. Des surfaces glacées devraient se former et pourraient être difficiles à repérer.

Veuillez continuer à surveiller les alertes et les prévisions émises par Environnement Canada. Pour signaler du temps violent, envoyez un courriel à meteoYT@ec.gc.ca ou publiez un message sur les réseaux sociaux en utilisant #YTMeteo.&lt;br&gt;Expires: 2026-11-07T02:20:51-00:00&lt;br&gt;Originated from CAP Alert: Environnement Canada, 2026-11-06T17:21:51-00:00, urn:oid:2.49.0.1.124.3601961978.2026&lt;br&gt;Area: Beaver Creek</summary><category term="status=Actual"/><category term="msgType=Alert"/><category term="scope=Public"/><category term="language=fr-CA"/><category term="category=Met"/><category term="severity=Moderate"/><category term="urgency=Immediate"/><category term="certainty=Likely"/><category term="event=bruine verglaçante"/></entry>
