 -126.6699 57.0477 -125.06 56.9999 -123.3 56.9577 -123.2874 56.3068 -122.6071 55.7116 -122.0337 55.5297 -121.839 55.38 -121.6999 55.1899 -122.0782 54.9999 -122.4999 54.848 -122.8357 54.7 -123.1999 54.655 -123.3415 54.615 -123.4872 55.067 -123.9108 55.1898 -124.1684 55.33 -124.4199 55.346 -124.4416</georss:polygon><summary type="html">Description: What:
Moderate to strong gusty winds.

When:
Now through late this evening.

Where:
- South Cariboo
- 100 Mile House (Including Highway 97)
- South Thompson
- Fraser Canyon - north including Lillooet
- Williston (Including Pine Pass)
- Yellowhead (near West Twin Creek)

Additional information:
A strong low pressure system approaching the B.C. coast is bringing a prolonged period of southeast winds with gusts ranging from 60-80 km/h to the B.C. interior. These southeast winds will peak this morning with the exception of South Thompson and Lilooet whose winds will peak this afternoon. Winds may ease slightly this afternoon before an incoming cold front will bring a strong push of southwest winds, with gusts potentially reaching 90 km/h between South Thompson and Mackenzie. 

Another potentially strong storm is set to follow on Saturday evening. 

Local utility outages are possible. Parks and forests may sustain damage. Secure loose objects.

###

